{:edb/db-before-t 1529 :edb/db-after-t 1530 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534842 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:43:33.670Z" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124112 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124112 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124112 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6fa2a35bd31547c7ee3931d9c21defc69be918fb57c8ceb26ce9f19e1a77c816.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124112 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{y + 1 \\ge 0; x + y \\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}\n$$" 13194139534842 false] [17592186124113 1100 "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124113 1100 "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124113 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b3e80f16cf1d83b9e6936a77fbd8c165a610bc5bff73b39521b03058e5b066b2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124113 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x + y > 0; \\ln (x + y) \\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,: \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain.\n\n- Starting with $y> -x$, we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1899/Source/Images/bcd5261dc88387b9f76d0ff643039167.png)" 13194139534842 false] [17592186124114 1100 "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n$f(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7)$.\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3)$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124114 1100 "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124114 1145 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3)$, we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(10, 3) &= (y^{2} - \\log_{3} (x - 7)) \\mid _{(10, 3)} \\\\\n&= 3^{2} - \\log_{3} (10 - 7) \\\\\n&= 9 - \\log_{3} (3) \\\\\n&= 9 - 1 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(10,3)=8\n$$" 13194139534842 false] [17592186124114 1145 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124116 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124116 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124116 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124116 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n${2x + y > 0; x > 0$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}\n$$" 13194139534842 false] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313941 13194139534842 true] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313976 13194139534842 true] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313983 13194139534842 true] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313990 13194139534842 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313948 13194139534842 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313955 13194139534842 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313962 13194139534842 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313969 13194139534842 true] [17592186124559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314004 13194139534842 true] [17592186124559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314018 13194139534842 true] [17592186124559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314032 13194139534842 true] [17592186124559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314039 13194139534842 true] [17592186124559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314046 13194139534842 true] [17592186124561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313997 13194139534842 true] [17592186124561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314011 13194139534842 true] [17592186124561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314025 13194139534842 true] [17592186124715 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534842 true] [17592186124715 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z = (\\ln (x + y))/(y)$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124715 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)}{y}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124715 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>0 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534842 true] [17592186124716 1100 "Find the domain of the function  $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x-y).$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124716 1100 "Find the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\arccos (x - y)$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124716 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1.$\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-1\\le x-y\\le 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124717 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534842 true] [17592186124717 1100 "Find the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\frac{xy}{x^{2} + y^{2}}$." 13194139534842 false] [17592186124717 1100 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124717 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124718 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534842 true] [17592186124718 1100 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2} - 1}$?" 13194139534842 false] [17592186124718 1100 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}?$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186124718 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $\\ge $ sign, the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ is part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a solid curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and shade the area *outside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/ba31bbc16c58860a4bc3c4d33ea1a61cb3d86d0e73d8aa6a67869b3e96a7fe32.png)" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313942 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1089 "q-158179" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1100 "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}.$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1113 #uuid "8ffc177d-b73e-54a6-8456-b4975b1494ac" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313941 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}.\n$$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313943 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313944 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313945 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313946 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313947 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1041 "selection" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313946 13194139534842 true] [17592186313942 1110 #uuid "29a1827a-34d3-5733-9df6-476434b30016" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313943 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534842 true] [17592186313943 1111 #uuid "cbf1b557-d5bb-5d33-8348-e4e43d82a976" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313944 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534842 true] [17592186313944 1111 #uuid "b4203380-9bf8-53df-94da-1c518f20f749" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313945 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<0}" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534842 true] [17592186313945 1111 #uuid "2074cbff-74d9-5585-b2e3-5546c96a7d07" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313946 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534842 true] [17592186313946 1111 #uuid "51aaf4e3-28c1-5d53-b891-0861b33e391d" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313947 1034 "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534842 true] [17592186313947 1111 #uuid "1b3337a9-e1b0-5c41-adef-a1e7cc733f92" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313949 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1089 "q-158193" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1100 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}?$" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1113 #uuid "784ae653-35b6-5020-84f0-16e9723eee86" 13194139534842 true] [17592186313948 1145 "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined for all points $(x,y)$ on the plane, hence the domain is the entire $xy$-plane. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e